From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crash-reporter: keep crashes of NickelOS local accounts

On NickelOS, Chrome and the session's apps run as the signed-in local
account (uid 5000-5999), not chronos. crash_reporter treated that uid like
a system daemon and chose /var/spool/crash, which the account cannot write;
when Chrome's crashpad called it, Chrome's sandbox (Landlock) blocked it
too. Every Chrome crash of a local account was lost, minidump and all.

A local account's crashes now go where chronos's go on a release image: the
account's own cryptohome, through daemon-store (/run/daemon-store/crash/
<hash>), also on test images. The directory is crash:crash-user-access,
sticky; local accounts are in crash-user-access like chronos, and can ask
session_manager for the active session like chronos.

---
diff -ruN a/crash-reporter/crash_collector.cc b/crash-reporter/crash_collector.cc
--- a/crash-reporter/crash_collector.cc
+++ b/crash-reporter/crash_collector.cc
@@ -132,6 +132,15 @@
 // Directory mode of the user crash spool directory.
 // This is SGID so that files created in it are also accessible to the group.
 const mode_t kUserCrashPathMode = 02770;
+
+// NickelOS local accounts (nickel-accounts) have uids in this range. Chrome
+// and the session's apps run as the signed-in account instead of chronos.
+constexpr uid_t kNickelFirstLocalUid = 5000;
+constexpr uid_t kNickelLastLocalUid = 5999;
+
+bool IsNickelLocalAccount(uid_t uid) {
+  return uid >= kNickelFirstLocalUid && uid <= kNickelLastLocalUid;
+}
 #endif
 
 // Directory mode of the system crash spool directory.
@@ -1138,7 +1147,22 @@
       return base::unexpected(
           CrashCollectionStatus::kFailedCrashUserGroupNameGroupInfo);
     }
-    std::optional<base::FilePath> maybe_path = GetUserCrashDirectoryNew();
+    std::optional<base::FilePath> maybe_path;
+    if (IsNickelLocalAccount(process_euid)) {
+      // NickelOS: a local account's crashes go to its own cryptohome
+      // (daemon-store), on test images too. The fallback directories belong
+      // to chronos or root, so the account could neither write nor fix them,
+      // and Chrome's crashes would be lost.
+      std::vector<FilePath> directories;
+      SetUpDBus();
+      if (util::GetDaemonStoreCrashDirectories(session_manager_proxy_.get(),
+                                                &directories) &&
+          !directories.empty()) {
+        maybe_path = directories[0];
+      }
+    } else {
+      maybe_path = GetUserCrashDirectoryNew();
+    }
     if (maybe_path) {
       // We *cannot* create or fix /run/daemon-store/crash/..., so don't try.
       // Only cryptohome's namespace mounter is capable of mounting it
